Liveblocks

presence-liveblocks uses @liveblocks/client and @liveblocks/react, both
Apache-2.0. @liveblocks/node is also Apache-2.0. It is documented in
registry/lib/presence/README.md for a host auth route and for server-side
agent presence. It is not a dependency of this repository.

@liveblocks/server and the liveblocks CLI are AGPL-3.0. They are not
dependencies, and this registry does not include them.

The Liveblocks Free plan needs a visible Liveblocks badge and allows 10
concurrent connections per room. Confirm the current plan limits before
shipping.

Supabase Realtime Presence uses @supabase/supabase-js, already used by the
admin adapter. Presence payloads are not an authorization source.
